# Expense Management System - Cursor Rules

## JSX Text Content

When writing JSX text content that includes special characters:

- **Quotes**: Use curly braces with template literals or string literals instead of escaping
  ```tsx
  // ✅ Good - use curly braces
  <p>{"We'll never share your email"}</p>
  <p>{`Don't worry about "quotes"`}</p>
  
  // ❌ Avoid - HTML entities are harder to read
  <p>We&apos;ll never share your email</p>
  <p>Don&apos;t worry about &quot;quotes&quot;</p>
  ```

- **Apostrophes**: Use curly braces for contractions
  ```tsx
  // ✅ Good
  <span>{"It's working"}</span>
  
  // ❌ Avoid
  <span>It&apos;s working</span>
  ```

## Component Patterns

### Client Components
- Add `'use client'` directive at the top of files that use React hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useRef`, etc.)
- Place the directive before all imports

### Import Organization
- Separate type imports from value imports for clarity
- Group imports: React → external libs → internal modules → types

```tsx
'use client';

import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import type { ReactNode } from 'react';

import { someLib } from 'external-lib';

import { Button } from '@/components/atoms';
import type { ButtonProps } from '@/components/atoms';
```

## Form Components

### Atoms (Basic Elements)
- Include `label`, `error`, `helperText`, and `isRequired` props
- Use `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby` for accessibility
- Support `forwardRef` for form library integration

### Molecules (Composite Components)
- Combine atoms into reusable form patterns
- Handle validation display
- Provide consistent spacing with FormField/FormRow

## Images

### When to use `next/image` vs native `<img>`

- **Use `next/image`** for static images, remote URLs, or any images that can be optimized
  ```tsx
  import Image from 'next/image';
  
  <Image src="/logo.png" alt="Logo" width={100} height={50} />
  <Image src="https://example.com/image.jpg" alt="Remote" width={200} height={200} />
  ```

- **Use native `<img>`** for blob URLs (from `URL.createObjectURL()`) - Next.js Image doesn't support these
  ```tsx
  // ✅ Correct - blob URLs require native img
  /* eslint-disable-next-line @next/next/no-img-element -- blob URLs not supported by next/image */
  <img src={blobUrl} alt="Preview" />
  ```

- Always add the eslint-disable comment with explanation when using `<img>`

## Testing

- Place tests in `__tests__` folder next to components
- Use `@testing-library/react` for component tests
- Mock file APIs when testing file upload components

## Multi-Tenancy

CRITICAL: Every database query MUST include `tenant_id` filtering.

